{"id": "tea:haribhaktivilasa:1", "source": "src:haribhaktivilasa", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The guru should be of good family and conduct, learned, pure, devoted and self-controlled, and the disciple sincere and faithful; each should examine the other before initiation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "devotion"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:gopala-bhatta-gosvami"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru-in-gaudiya"], "notes": "Vilāsa-level reference.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:haribhaktivilasa:11", "source": "src:haribhaktivilasa", "location": {"ref": "11"}, "paraphrase": "Surrender (śaraṇāgati) has six limbs: resolving to do what is favourable, giving up what is unfavourable, faith that he will protect, choosing him as protector, offering oneself, and humility.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:gopala-bhatta-gosvami"], "practices": ["prc:prapatti"], "terms": ["trm:saranagati"], "notes": "Vilāsa-level reference; the verse is shared with Pāñcarātra sources.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:haribhaktivilasa:12-13", "source": "src:haribhaktivilasa", "location": {"ref": "12-13"}, "paraphrase": "The fast of Ekādaśī (Hari's day) is obligatory for Vaiṣṇavas; the rules of the fast, of its breaking and of festival days are laid down.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:gopala-bhatta-gosvami"], "practices": ["prc:ekadasi-vrata"], "notes": "Vilāsa-level reference.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:haribhaktivilasa:2", "source": "src:haribhaktivilasa", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "Initiation (dīkṣā) is so called because it gives divine knowledge and destroys sin; by it the disciple receives the mantra and becomes fit for deity worship.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "sound"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "sound-language"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:gopala-bhatta-gosvami"], "practices": ["prc:gaudiya-diksa"], "terms": ["trm:diksa"], "notes": "Vilāsa-level reference; the dīkṣā mantras are not reproduced.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
